Network Information Technology (NIT) provides easy to administer
mainframe-quality security for UNIX and NT multiplatform environments.
Security policy enforcement is transparent to end-users and scalable
enterprise-wide.  

----------

UniShield offers access control to sensitive files and critical
applications; centralized password management, privilege delegation,
real-time intrusion detection and alert, and customizable audit reporting.
It protects web servers, file servers, and database servers including
Netscape, NFS, and Oracle.

UniShield is comprised of five security software modules which operate as
stand alone products or as a fully integrated suite.  This modular approach
gives you the option of implementing various levels of security in phases.
Each UniShield 3.0 security software module is briefly described below:

* Enterprise Security Administrator (ESA) - Provides a set of base-line
  authentication and authorization security functions.  It also delivers
  account management functionality for adding, deleting, and configuring user
  accounts.

* File Access Control (FAC) - Secures and authorizes access to files and
  programs.  FAC protects sensitive data in addition to critical web server,
  file server, and database server applications such as Netscape, NFS, and 
  Oracle.

* Administrative Privilege Delegation (APD) - Delegates a subset of the
  Superuser administrative powers (or other privileged user capabilities)
  without giving away full root power or disclosing the root password.

* Advanced Security Monitor (ASM) - Transparently audits and monitors
  selective operating system events and user keystrokes without interfering
  with system operations.

* Single Sign-On (SSO), (under development) - Provides a secured single user
