>Thanx in advance for any ideas.....

No ideas, simply quoting the csh online manual:

"If csh runs as a login shell, it executes commands from the
system-wide login file /etc/csh.login, if that file exists, and the
commands from your $HOME/.cshrc file and your $HOME/.login file, in
that order."

You may also change the default login files in /usr/skel.

Matthias
